From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: harden EDMA lifecycle

Several EDMA error and teardown paths operate on resources which were
never acquired or have already been released.

The ring allocation rollback loops use unsigned indices with conditions
which can never become false after underflow.  IRQ registration failures
similarly free every configured IRQ rather than only those successfully
requested, while IRQ lookup returns an error through an array after
freeing that array.  The port teardown path deletes NAPI and frees
per-CPU statistics before unregister_netdev() has stopped all users.

Track the exact IRQ resources acquired, preserve lookup errors before
freeing their storage, and unwind rings with bounded reverse loops.
Stop a netdevice before deleting its NAPI instance and freeing its
statistics.  Also disable the correct per-port TX rings, balance EDMA
clock enables with device-managed actions, validate the EDMA child node,
and route hardware/setup failures through complete cleanup paths.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
